      <Comment source="SRI, caspi">Mercapturic acids are S-conjugates of |FRAME: CPD-9175|, which are formed in the liver and excreted in the urine. In the process of generating a mercapturic acid, a compound is first conjugated with glutathione. This is followed by loss of the glutamate and glycine portions, followed by acetylation of the L-cysteine nitrogen to form the mercapturic acid.</Comment>
